ROLE: You make literal edits to two TypeScript files. Re-read each first. Make exactly these edits and nothing else.

CONTEXT: An OpenCode 1 tool resolves to a string or to `{ title?, output, metadata?, attachments? }`, where each attachment is `{ type: "file", mime, url, filename? }`. OpenCode 2's tool result is `{ content?, metadata? }`, where `content` is a string or an array of `{ type: "text", text }` and `{ type: "file", uri, mime, name? }` items.

ACTION:

1. In `.skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime/src/opencode/tools.ts`, replace this block:

/** A tool in the shape OpenCode 2's tool editor accepts. */
export interface V2ToolDefinition {
  readonly name: string;
  readonly description: string;
  readonly input: unknown;
  readonly execute: (input: unknown) => Promise<{ readonly content: string }>;
}

with:

/** One item of an OpenCode 2 tool result's content. */
export type V2ToolContent =
  | { readonly type: "text"; readonly text: string }
  | { readonly type: "file"; readonly uri: string; readonly mime: string; readonly name?: string };

/** A tool in the shape OpenCode 2's tool editor accepts. */
export interface V2ToolDefinition {
  readonly name: string;
  readonly description: string;
  readonly input: unknown;
  readonly execute: (input: unknown) => Promise<{
    readonly content: string | readonly V2ToolContent[];
    readonly metadata?: Readonly<Record<string, unknown>>;
  }>;
}

2. In the same file, replace these two lines inside `toV2Tools`:

      const result = await definition.execute(input as never, undefined as never);
      return { content: typeof result === "string" ? result : result.output };

with:

      const result = await definition.execute(input as never, undefined as never);
      if (typeof result === "string") return { content: result };
      const files: V2ToolContent[] = (result.attachments ?? []).map((attachment) => ({
        type: "file",
        uri: attachment.url,
        mime: attachment.mime,
        ...(attachment.filename ? { name: attachment.filename } : {}),
      }));
      return {
        content: files.length > 0 ? [{ type: "text", text: result.output }, ...files] : result.output,
        ...(result.metadata ? { metadata: result.metadata } : {}),
      };

3. In `.skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime/src/opencode/tools.test.ts`, directly before the final line `});` of the file (the line that closes `describe("toV2Tools", () => {`), insert this test:

  it("carries an object result's metadata and attachments into the OpenCode 2 result", async () => {
    const v1 = {
      sk_vision_status: {
        description: "status",
        args: {},
        execute: async () => ({
          output: "ok",
          metadata: { device: "cpu" },
          attachments: [{ type: "file" as const, mime: "image/png", url: "file:///tmp/a.png", filename: "a.png" }],
        }),
      },
    } as unknown as Parameters<typeof toV2Tools>[0];
    const [status] = toV2Tools(v1);
    expect(await status?.execute({})).toEqual({
      content: [
        { type: "text", text: "ok" },
        { type: "file", uri: "file:///tmp/a.png", mime: "image/png", name: "a.png" },
      ],
      metadata: { device: "cpu" },
    });
  });

FORMAT: Then run `cd .skilled/skills/sk-vision/vision-runtime && bunx tsc --noEmit; echo typecheck-exit=$?; bun test src/opencode/tools.test.ts 2>&1 | tail -4` and print the output verbatim, nothing else.
